WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.120
A man named Eric is on a walk with his dog, Nova.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.340
While on the walk, Eric loses Nova

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.360
after she pulls the leash from his hand in pursuit of a rabbit

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.320
that happens to jump out of a bush as they pass by it.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.420
Eric chases after Nova but this only inspires her to run faster,

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.575
until she completely eludes Eric's vision

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.460
continuing on her pursuit of the rabbit, that has, by now,

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.220
hidden somewhere in the other direction.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.260
After a great deal of time passes, it becomes clear that Nova

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.000
has outrun her sense of orientation and is now lost.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.600
Eric spends the rest of the day and the days following

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.360
searching for Nova. He notifies neighbors,

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.640
enlists friends and family to help,

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.820
puts up signs, and so on.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.300
A week goes by,

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.460
nova is still missing eric is devastated beyond comprehension

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.000
 

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.940
he thinks

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.015
about how horribly unlucky it was that the rabbit

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:52.025
jumped out at just the wrong time his hand position

00:00:52.025 --> 00:00:54.860
just in the wrong place to allow Nova to pull the leash from it

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.600
About another week later, a woman shows up at Eric's front door,

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.180
she has Nova.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:05.260
After nova and Eric reconnect in a chaotic, heart-warming display of affection,

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.720
Eric thanks the woman.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.480
She introduces herself and tells Eric her name is Vanessa.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.780
She's beautiful, and about Eric's same age.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.200
Eric and Vanessa talk for a little while and seem to hit it off,

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.975
In the following weeks they hang out several times

00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:21.965
and things goes so well, they soon begin dating.

00:01:21.965 --> 00:01:24.985
Eric finds her to be absolutely gorgeous, kind, funny,

00:01:24.985 --> 00:01:28.120
smart, spontaneous... all the right buzzwords for a perfect

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.240
romantic partner in a story.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.340
Soon, Eric and Vanessa fall in love,

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.340
the relationship is everything one could reasonably hope a relationship to be.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.980
erick thinks about how lucky it was that vanessa was

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.020
who happend to be in the right place at the right time

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.420
to find and return Nova

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.160
A couple months go by,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.140
Eric is driving on his way to pick up Vanessa.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.320
While driving through an intersection, Eric is T-boned at full speed

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.480
by a driver who distractedly runs a red light

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.980
coming from the perpendicular side street.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.360
Eric is knocked unconscious as he and his car are sent in a

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.400
thrashing 1080° spin.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.160
An hour or so later, Eric finds himself in a hospital.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.000
A doctor informs Eric of what has happened, and explains

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.860
that he has suffered a severe head injury, and that they will need to run

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.480
some immediate tests as well as a brain scan to determine the severity,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.140
and if there's any chance of permanent brain damage

00:02:18.145 --> 00:02:19.195
or internal bleeding.

00:02:19.595 --> 00:02:22.485
As his consciousness begins to more clearly return to him,

00:02:22.735 --> 00:02:25.795
Erick thinks about how unlucky it was to been going

00:02:25.795 --> 00:02:28.735
to get Vanessa in the exact direction at the exact time

00:02:28.985 --> 00:02:32.225
 

00:02:32.225 --> 00:02:34.885
 

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.020
Eric is held overnight at the hospital.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.880
The next day, the doctor comes in into Eric's room:

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.060
, the doctor asks.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.200
, Eric replies.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.175
 

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.000
, they doctor says.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.620
, Eric responds.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.720
 

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.540
Confused, Eric says:

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.040
 

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:06.540
, says the doctor.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.520
 

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.340
, Eric asks with an escalating level of concern and confusion.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.560
 

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.880
The doctor pauses for a moment,

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.840
and Eric looks at him unaware of what this means.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.640
"It's a tumor", the doctor goes on to saying

00:03:22.645 --> 00:03:25.635
 

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.080
 

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.080
, Eric asks.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.840
 

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.420
 

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.200
"... we ran the brain scan. Because of the brain scan

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.520
we found the tumor. Normally we only catch a tumor like this

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.600
 

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.600
"... Because we found the tumor right now, though,

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.640
we cut it while it's still benign before it became malignant

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.220
and grew into any other areas of your brain,

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.820
which in almost all cases becomes fatal.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.720
Since it's still in this stage, though, we should be able to remove it almost entirely

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.940
without any issue.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.255
 

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.720
 

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.500
, the doctor concludes.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.740
Eric starts to feel a weird, visceral tingling sensation

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.880
and becomes slightly disoriented.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.880
 

00:04:22.885 --> 00:04:25.635
 

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:29.040
 

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.940
Regardless, Eric looks around at the room.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.740
He thinks about how lucky he was

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.600
to having going to get Vanessa in the exact direction

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.220
at that exact time. He thinks about how lucky he was

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.360
to have gotten in the car accident.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.740
He thinks about how weird it is to think this.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.620
In this moment, Eric realizes how little he knows

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.640
about what anything actually is.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:58.380
That he has never and can never know what exists on the other side of

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.180
anything that happens to him or because of him,

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.040
no matter how good or bad, lucky or unlucky

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.580
any of it might seem.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:09.460
Eric feels a strange, paradoxical sense of helplessness

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.880
and liberation.

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.440
About a week later,  Eric undergoes brain surgery to remove the tumor.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.120
The surgery is successful.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:21.040
Eric is mostly as good as new, with exception to a scar running down the side of his scalp

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.900
Several days later, after being released from the hospital,

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.580
Eric is at home with Vanessa, recovering.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.040
To get some fresh air,

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.040
he takes Nova out for a walk.

